WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.327
"Are Plant Sterols Safe for Lowering Cholesterol?"

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:09.360
According to an expert
consensus statement

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.000
from the European
Atherosclerosis Society,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.600
at the recommended daily intake

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.920
of two grams
of plant sterols a day,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.000
the available evidence
does not suggest

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.360
any adverse effect associated
with long-term intake.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.920
And evidence from animal
and cell studies suggests

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:26.400
a protective role
of plant sterol intake

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.080
and risk of certain cancers.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.480
Human population studies
have also found

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.360
a protective effect
of dietary phytosterol intake

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.640
on cancer risk;

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:35.760
those who consumed the most

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.040
had a 37% lower risk of cancer.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.120
But where are
phytosterols found?

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.600
Healthy foods
like nuts and seeds.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.440
Even just a single ounce
of nuts (30 g) a day

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.680
is associated
with less cardiovascular risk

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.080
and a lower risk of dying
from cancer

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.800
and from dying
from all causes put together.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.880
So, phytosterols
may just be a marker

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.440
for healthy food intake,
though it's also possible

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.280
that phytosterols may be
one of the reasons

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.600
nuts and seeds
are so good for us.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.000
There's a new class
of anti-cancer agents

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.160
known as histone
deacetylase inhibitors,

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.600
available for the low, low cost
of $38,000 a month,

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:14.560
but in terms of the most potent
naturally occurring

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.320
such inhibitors
reported to date,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.720
phytosterols may fit the bill,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:19.840
perhaps one of the reasons

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.960
healthy plant foods
are so good for us.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:24.800
Post-marketing
surveillance studies

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.640
are said to have given
phytosterols

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:28.000
a clean bill of health

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.720
based on thousands
of consumers,

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.560
but the study was done
by the company

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.840
that sells those products;

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.960
so, I don't take
much comfort from it.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.480
There's a concern
that plant sterols

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:39.600
could reduce the absorption

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.400
of certain fat-soluble vitamins.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.120
They don't seem to impact
concentrations of blood levels

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.200
of vitamins A, D, or K,

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.960
but they can drop
vitamin E levels by about 10%.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:52.960
The main concern, though,
has been about the loss

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.440
of carotenoids
like beta carotene.

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:58.400
One modeling study suggested
that if margarines became

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.880
a hundred percent fortified
with phytosterols,

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:03.280
the incidence
of night blindness—

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:05.360
difficulty seeing in dim light—

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:09.680
may increase as much as 19
in a thousand every year,

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.640
whereas that would also result
in one in a thousand

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:14.320
not getting heart disease.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.240
Since night blindness
is considered

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.480
a relatively minor
visual disturbance,

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.400
the benefits of fortification

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.680
might clearly outweigh
the putative risk,

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.600
but there's no need
to have any risk at all,

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.360
because the relatively small
suppression

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:30.240
of plasma carotenoid levels
can be countered

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.440
by just eating more fruits
and vegetables.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.960
The problem
with fortifying something

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.640
like margarine
with phytosterols

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:38.240
is that people
may cook with it,

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.320
and that could cause
the plant sterols to oxidize

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.040
into phytosterol
oxidation products.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.560
We know cholesterol oxidation
products are particularly bad,

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:49.920
but we aren't sure
about oxidized phytosterols.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.320
We don't know enough about
what happens when we heat them;

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.760
so, better safe than sorry.

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.600
Don't cook with
phytosterol-fortified products.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.600
There was
a concerning finding in rats,

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.120
where phytosterols
were found to make

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.400
their red blood cells
more fragile,

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:07.120
but in mice,
the opposite was found—

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.440
their red blood cells
became less fragile,

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.480
and in hamsters, there didn't
seem to be any effect.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:17.200
So, are we more like rats,
mice, or hamsters?

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.400
Now, the amount of plant sterols
researchers used in the rats

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.680
was, like, 50 times higher
than you'd see in people,

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:26.320
but you really don't know
what normal amounts can do

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:29.680
until you put it to the test,

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:32.960
and it turns out that doesn't
appear to be an issue.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.760
There is, however,
a rare genetic condition

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.280
called phytosterolemia,

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.360
where people end up
with extremely high levels

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.720
of phytosterols in their blood

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:45.440
and end up with horrific
heart disease, even as kids.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.120
But the same mutations
that allow

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.360
for the increased absorption
of phytosterols

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.320
also allow for the increased
absorption of cholesterol;

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:54.720
so, these unfortunate kids
end up with cholesterol levels

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:56.400
in the 700s.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.720
No wonder they're dying
of heart attacks.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.200
So, when those
who just genetically end up

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.640
with higher levels
of phytosterols

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:04.080
in their bloodstream
have higher rates

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.760
of cardiovascular disease,

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:08.160
it's not necessarily
because plant sterols

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:10.240
increase the risk
of coronary heart disease,

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.520
as some had feared,

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.080
but rather because those people
are also sucking up

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:16.480
extra regular cholesterol.

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:19.280
These genetic variations
in sterol transporters,

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.160
result in increased blood levels
of phytosterols,

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.640
increased intestinal
cholesterol absorption

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.360
and subsequently result
in higher LDL.

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.200
In fact, that's how we estimate

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.680
how good people are
at absorbing cholesterol,

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.760
by just seeing
how many plant sterols

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.200
they have in their blood.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.440
So, people with lots
of phytosterols in their blood

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:40.240
also have markedly elevated
LDL cholesterol.

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:43.280
No wonder they're at risk
for heart disease.

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.000
However, this increase
in cholesterol absorption

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.640
doesn't fully explain
the increased risk;

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:50.000
so, it's possible

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.320
that phytosterols
may indeed contribute

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:54.000
directly to heart disease,

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.680
raising questions
about the safety

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.520
of supplementing food
with phytosterols

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:00.880
for the purpose of
cardiovascular risk reduction.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:03.440
But the risk in LDL
achieved by the consumption

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:08.000
of phytosterol-enriched foods
is 20 to 40 times greater

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.640
than the increase
in phytosterols in the blood.

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.520
Thus, phytosterols would need
to cause 20 to 40 times

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:15.680
more atherosclerosis
than cholesterol

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.280
to cancel out
their positive effect

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.640
on cholesterol reduction.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.280
Yet, there is
no apparent evidence for this.

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.040
In fact, at the levels
we get in our blood

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:26.320
from consuming a few grams
of plant sterols a day,

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:29.200
there is no association
with cardiovascular events

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.560
in population studies.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.720
So, that's how you get
these assurances

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:37.092
that phytosterols are safe.

